@startuml possession-flow
' ⚠ RENDERING: this diagram is ~9,600px tall as of §3.14b, which is PAST
' PlantUML's default 4096px ceiling — `plantuml -tpng` SILENTLY TRUNCATES it
' to the top ~43% with no warning. Always render with:
'
'   plantuml -DPLANTUML_LIMIT_SIZE=16384 -tpng docs/possession-flow.puml
'
' `plantuml -checkonly` is unaffected (it parses, it does not lay out), so a
' green checkonly does NOT tell you the PNG is complete. Verify the rendered
' height if you add a partition.
title Possession Resolution (§3.2–§3.5, §3.7 blocks, §3.8 missed-shot OOB,\n§3.9 turnover causes, §3.10 rebounding fouls + bonus, §3.11 and-1,\n§3.12 all-shot-type contact fouls, §3.13 foul trouble, §3.14a technicals,\n§3.14b flagrants, §3.16 shooting-foul composition + charges)

skinparam ActivityDiamondFontSize 11
skinparam ActivityFontSize 12
skinparam NoteFontSize 10

start

note right
  **§3.4 coach pace** scales the possession COUNT
  (loop bound), blended across both coaches.
end note

partition "RotationState — between-possession sub (§3.5, §3.13, §3.14a)" {
  :drain on-floor energy (× endurance)
  recover benched energy;
  if (**§3.14a — technical foul?**\n//P = TECHNICAL_FOULS_PER_TEAM_GAME ÷ nominal checks//\nrolled PER TEAM, no causal model at all) then (yes)
    :FOUL — TECHNICAL_FOUL
    committer: //foulProne//-weighted draw
    over the ON-FLOOR FIVE only;
    :**1 free throw** to the other team
    shooter = highest //freeThrows// on the floor
    (DETERMINISTIC — consumes no RNG);
    note right
      **§3.14a (#032 B/C/D/E/G) — the foul with NO contest behind it.**
      Every other foul in this engine is a by-product of a contest
      (pickDefender → isFoul). A technical is **behavioral**, so it
      hangs off nothing — which is exactly why it is rolled HERE,
      between possessions, and **NOT** on the possession path.
      **THE POSSESSION IS UNCHANGED** (D) — no fork, no retention,
      no switch, even when the offense commits it. §3.14a adds
      **NO branch below this partition**; if you are looking for one,
      there isn't one, and that is the design.
      **Its own counter** (E): does NOT feed FOUL_OUT_LIMIT, does NOT
      feed foulTroubleLevel(), and is EXCLUDED from the period bonus
      tally — #028 A1's first outcome-aware exception.
      **Committer is on-floor only** (C): the bench is excluded to
      avoid spending ~2/3 of the rate on players whose technicals
      have no engine consequence. foulProne is nearly flat (sd 1.22),
      so the draw is near-uniform — accepted, because the RATE is a
      fixed constant and the weighting moves no aggregate.
      **No PROB_FLOOR** (H): the floor (0.02) is more than **10×**
      the per-check rate (**~0.00175**) — it would inflate technicals
      by that factor. Routed through the shared floor-free clamp
      helper (`clampRareProbability`) this pass added.
      //Execution correction: #032 B2 estimated the per-check rate at//
      //~0.0035 off ~100 checks per team-game. The true count is ~200 —//
      //BOTH rotations advance on EVERY possession — so the rate is half//
      //that. The game-level constant (0.35) is unchanged.//
      //The roll and committer draw live in RotationState; the EVENT and//
      //the FT are emitted by PossessionEngine, which owns GameData, the//
      //team ids, the period and the sequence. advancePossession returns//
      //the committer.//
    end note
  else (no)
  endif
  :**hard** — force off any fouled-out OR ejected player
  //isFouledOut() || isEjected() || isEjectedForFlagrant()//
  //(fouls >= 6 · technicalFouls >= 2 · flagrantTwos >= 1)//
  → sub from full roster;
  :**soft** — foul-trouble sub (§3.13)
  //P = base(fouls) × subAggressiveness × value × roster//
  from //rotationDepth// window only; yields if bench can't cover;
  :fatigue sub — pull most-tired starter below
  //subAggressiveness// threshold for freshest bench
  within //rotationDepth//; starters pulled later / return first;
  note right
    Three tiers: **hard/forced · soft/preference · fatigue**
    (#031 H). **§3.14a's ejection extends the HARD tier via
    the `eligible(...)` filter — NOT a fourth removal path.**
    It stays **DERIVED** (//technicalFouls >= 2//, a monotonic
    counter — #023 F applies unchanged, #032 F).
    **§3.14b adds a THIRD cause to the SAME predicate**
    (//flagrantTwos >= 1//) — still not a fourth path, and
    still **DERIVED**. #031 H / #032 F predicted a flagrant-2
    would finally force stored state; **it does not** (#034 F):
    a flagrant-2 ejects IMMEDIATELY, so there is no threshold
    to remember and the counter is monotonic like the other
    two. **Every disqualification here is absorbing — which
    is exactly the shape #023 F's derivation was built for.
    The stored-state prediction is RETIRED, not deferred.**
    Flagrant ejections land ~0.024/team/game — roughly DOUBLE
    §3.14a's 0.014, so this tier is finally exercised.
    **Consumes THREE RNG draws** — §3.13's sit roll, §3.14a's
    technical roll, and §3.14a's committer draw, ALL taken
    unconditionally at fixed points so the stream never forks
    on rotation state (decisions.md #031, revising #023 C's
    RNG-free sub). The committer draw is drawn even on the
    ~99.8% of calls that don't need it, precisely to keep the
    count state-independent. //(Execution: THREE, not the TWO//
    //the design pass drew — the committer draw was made//
    //unconditional for the same fixed-point reason.)//
    The step itself emits no events: it RETURNS the technical's
    committer and PossessionEngine emits the FOUL + free throw.
    The soft rule protects the BEST players MORE — the
    deliberate inverse of the fatigue rule's starter
    tolerance. Sticky sit: return is EARNED via the
    fatigue freshness path, never re-rolled.
    onFloor() is always exactly 5 (least-fouled stays
    as last resort). A fouled-out player NEVER returns.
  end note
}

repeat
:ShotSelector
  pick shooter (offensive-weight draw)
  pick shot type (skill-weight draw
  //× offensiveScheme shot-mix lean §3.4//);

partition "TurnoverResolver (§3.9 causes — decisions.md #027)" {
  if (turnover?\n//ballSecurity vs stealing/individualDefense//\n//× defensiveScheme pressure §3.4//\n//× fatigueFactor per player §3.5//) then (yes)
    note right
      **The gate above is UNCHANGED by §3.9** (#027 A) — a turnover
      happens exactly as often as before. Only AFTER a turnover is
      declared does a weighted draw pick WHICH of NINE causes it was,
      so the draw re-partitions the label without moving the count.
      That is what made §3.9 free by construction.
      Leans (#027 C): SHOT_CLOCK_VIOLATION on //acumen//↓ ×
      //defensiveScheme//↑; OFFENSIVE_FOUL / BAD_PASS on //teamOffense//↓.
      STOLEN stays dominant. Every cause charges the ball-handler.
    end note
    if (cause == STOLEN?\n//weighted nine-way draw//) then (yes)
      :TURNOVER — STOLEN
      credit defender steal;
    else (no)
      :TURNOVER — one of
      SHOT_CLOCK_VIOLATION / OFFENSIVE_FOUL / BAD_PASS /
      TRAVELLING / LOST_BALL_OUT_OF_BOUNDS / 3_SECONDS_VIOLATION /
      8_SECONDS_BACKCOURT_VIOLATION / OVER_AND_BACK
      //no stealer credited//;
      if (**§3.16 — cause == OFFENSIVE_FOUL?**\n//the charge / illegal screen — a PERSONAL FOUL by rule//) then (yes)
        :FOUL — OFFENSIVE_FOUL
        charge the BALL-HANDLER //recordFoul()// (G)
        committingTeamId = **OFFENSE** — so the DEFENSE gains the bonus;
        note right
          **§3.16 (decisions.md #039 G) — the charge correctness fix (#037).**
          ⚠ **TWO EVENTS FOR ONE OCCURRENCE**: the TURNOVER above and this
          FOUL both describe the same charge. Any reconciliation that counts
          events must tolerate that, and the harness's ``Fouls / team / game``
          line steps up **~1.26 for this reason alone** — NOT the §3.16
          re-partition misfiring.
          Before §3.16 ``recordFoul()`` was **never called** here, so a charge
          counted toward nothing: not the committer's six, not the team-foul
          tally, not the box-score ``fouls`` column (#027 never considered it).
          **This is the ONLY site where the committer is on OFFENSE outside the
          rebounding foul**, so it is the only other path that puts the
          DEFENSIVE team in the bonus. ``GameData.isInBonus`` reads
          ``committingTeamId`` and already supports it.
          **NOT flagrant-eligible** (#039 G) — the flagrant roll lives in
          FoulResolver and this path never reaches it. Counts toward the
          bonus and FOUL_OUT_LIMIT: it is a personal foul.
          The possession already ends (it is a turnover), so #039 C's
          possession question does not arise here.
        end note
      endif
    endif
    stop
  endif
}

partition "FoulResolver" {
  note right
    **§3.12 (decisions.md #030 A1/A2) — SHIPPED.**
    The binary ``ShotType.isContactType()`` gate that stood here
    (DRIVE or POST?) is **DELETED**. **Every** shot type can now be
    fouled, graduated by a per-shot-type multiplier on the base
    constant: DRIVE 1.0 (the anchor) ≈ POST > PERIMETER > THREE.
    That base is **UNTOUCHED at 0.15** and still means "P(contact
    stops the shot)" **on a drive**, so drive/post rates stay
    numerically identical to §3.11 and the whole §3.12 delta is
    attributable to the two newly foulable types (A2).
    It is **RENAMED ``BASE_FOUL`` → ``BASE_NO_BASKET_FOUL``** (F) —
    value unchanged; it never meant "the foul rate", it means the
    foul STOPPED the shot, which is exactly why trimming it moves
    points the WRONG way (see the legend).
    A multiplier of 0.0 — not a zero base — is the only true
    off-switch (the #029 zero-base finding).
  end note
  if (foul?\n//foulDrawing vs (20 − foulProne)//\n//× foulMultiplier(shotType) §3.12 A1//\n//× fatigueFactor per player §3.5//) then (yes)
    :FOUL — SHOOTING_FOUL
    charge defender foul;
    note right
      foul rate × defensiveScheme pressure §3.4.
      This is the **pre-shot** foul — the shot is stopped,
      a 2-FT trip (**3 on a THREE**, §3.12 C), mutually
      exclusive with a made basket. The **and-1** (foul WITH
      a made shot) is a separate post-make roll (§3.11,
      inside SHOT — MADE below).
      **NB the stopped shot charges NO FGA** — this branch
      returns before recordFieldGoalAttempt() — so it removes
      points without moving FG% directly, but it DOES change
      the shot mix FG% is computed over (§3.12 E).
    end note

    if (**§3.14b — FLAGRANT?**\n//P = FLAGRANT_FOULS_PER_TEAM_GAME ÷ personal fouls//\n//layered ON TOP of the foul — no rate re-partitioned//) then (yes)
      :FOUL — FLAGRANT_FOUL_1 or _2
      //15% severity sub-roll (#034 E) — flat, no causal input//
      charge committer //recordFoul()// — a PERSONAL foul (I)
      on _2: //recordFlagrantTwo()// → EJECTED;
      :FREE_THROW ×**2** — *_FLAGRANT (new source)
      the FOULED player shoots (D)
      **REPLACES the 2/3 FTs above — does NOT add** (C);
      note right
        **§3.14b (#034 A/B/C) — THE POSSESSION-RETENTION FORK,
        and the first FT path in this engine that does NOT end
        the possession** (breaking #030 B's invariant).
        A defensive flagrant returns the ball: the offense
        **RE-ENTERS the second-chance loop** — the SAME
        ``offensiveRebounds++; continue;`` §3.7/§3.8/§3.10 use,
        under the SAME MAX_OFFENSIVE_RETENTIONS cap (B). No new
        mechanism: the loop already IS "same team, run it again".
        This site is **always defensive**, so it always retains.
        ⚠ **The terminator below is NOT "possession over"** — it is where
        this branch leaves the diagram to re-enter the loop at ShotSelector.
        Activity-diagram syntax cannot draw an edge back into the enclosing
        ``repeat`` from inside a partition, so retention is shown as the
        labelled step above rather than as a drawn arrow. **Every other
        ``stop`` on this page really does end the possession; these three
        flagrant ones do not.**
      end note
      :→ **OFFENSE RETAINS** → ``offensiveRebounds++; continue;``
      re-enter the second-chance loop at ShotSelector (B)
      //(unless the cap is already reached — then the possession ends,//
      //the FTs having been awarded either way, exactly as §3.10 degrades)//;
      stop
    endif

    if (**§3.16 — COMMON (non-shooting) FOUL?**\n//flat sim.non-shooting-foul-share, NO skill input (#039 E)//\n//a SECOND roll on the foul already charged above//) then (yes)
      :FOUL — COMMON_FOUL
      //the foul was ALREADY charged above — this only re-labels it//
      counts toward the bonus AND FOUL_OUT_LIMIT (B);
      note right
        **§3.16 (decisions.md #039 A/B/C/D) — THE FTA RE-PARTITION,
        and the whole point of the phase.**
        **Layered, not carved** — the ``isFoul`` roll above is UNCHANGED
        in rate, skills and RNG draw, and ``recordFoul()`` has already
        run, so **the foul TOTAL holds by construction** (A). Exactly the
        ``isFlagrant`` shape three lines up (#034 A) and §3.9's turnover
        causes one layer out (#027 A).
        **Order matters**: flagrant is rolled FIRST, so a flagrant common
        foul is simply a flagrant (F) — the two never compose.
        ⚠ **THE POSSESSION ENDS AND THE BALL DOES NOT COME BACK (C), AND
        THAT IS DELIBERATELY WRONG AS BASKETBALL.** A real common foul is
        a side inbound: the offense keeps the ball. It is not modelled
        that way because **every returning variant yields a live attempt
        worth ~0.76 FGA where the stopped shot charged NONE**, and FGA is
        88.4 against 89.1 real — **0.7 of headroom**. That caps a
        retaining variant at a **~6% share**, which moves FTA by less
        than 1.0. The retention reading and the phase goal are
        arithmetically incompatible; FGA wins because it is sourced and
        already correct.
        **Share 0.50, and it is BACK-SOLVED, NOT SOURCED (D)** — the real
        NBA shooting-foul share is not in a league-averages row. The
        earlier ~35% figure is **withdrawn**: it assumed zero FTs, but a
        large share of these fouls are committed **ALREADY IN THE PENALTY**
        and those award 2 bonus FTs. #039 D predicted 0.43 from an 18.5%
        in-penalty share; the charge fork above raised the bonus rate to
        ~56% of team-periods, so each conversion removes ~1.47 FTs and the
        share measured out at **0.50** (5 seeds, FTA 23.6). The LANDING is
        the target, not the constant.
        ⚠ **Points falls ~8 to ~110 and §3.19 RECOVERS IT (H)** — not
        drift, and NOT to be chased here (#038's rule).
      end note
      if (committing team already in the penalty?\n//GameData.isInBonus — emit-then-count, §3.10 #028 A1//) then (yes)
        :FREE_THROW ×**2** — BONUS
        //the fouled team shoots; this is the 18.5% case above//;
      else (no)
        :**no free throws** — the point of the phase;
      endif
      stop
    endif

    repeat
      if (free throw made?\n//freeThrows skill//) then (yes)
        :FREE_THROW — MADE_SHOOTING (source-tagged §3.11 D)
        +1 point;
      else (no)
        :FREE_THROW — MISSED_SHOOTING;
      endif
    repeat while (shotType.freeThrowsIfFouled() done?\n//§3.12 C: 3 for THREE, else 2//) is (no) not (yes)
    note right
      **§3.12 C — the latent fouled-three fix.** The count is a
      RULE on ShotType (``freeThrowsIfFouled()``), not a SimConfig
      tunable, threaded through #029 D's already-parameterized
      ``awardFreeThrows`` — a call-site change, no new plumbing.
      A stopped THREE = **3** FTs; it never fired before only
      because THREE wasn't a contact type. No new FreeThrowSource:
      these are SHOOTING FTs, there are simply three of them.
      **§3.14b (#034 C): if this foul turned FLAGRANT the count
      becomes a flat 2 — so a flagrant stopped THREE awards FEWER
      FTs than the ordinary foul it upgraded. Correct by rule,
      counter-intuitive, and NOT to be "fixed" into 3 + 2.**
    end note
    stop
  endif
}

partition "ShotResolver" {
  :record FGA (+ 3PA if THREE);

  if (BLOCKED? //§3.7 — decisions.md #025//\n//P(BLOCK) carved off the top (A1), then MAKE/MISS on remainder//\n//contest: defender rimProtection (rim) / shotContest (jumper)//\n//vs shooter finishing (B2); own BLOCK_SENSITIVITY, THREE very-low (C)//\n//× fatigueFactor per player §3.5//) then (yes)
    :SHOT — BLOCKED_*
    event: PlayType.SHOT, outcome BLOCKED_* (F1)
    primaryPlayerId = shooter (the victim)
    shooter charged missed FGA (+3PA if THREE), 0 FGM (F3)
    blocker.recordBlock() — separate credit, not on event (F2)
    no assistPlayerId (F4);
    note right
      **Block = a field-goal outcome, exactly as a steal is a
      turnover outcome** (§3.2: TURNOVER/STOLEN + recordSteal).
      v3: one three-way MAKE/MISS/BLOCK draw — no double-count
      (probs sum to 1). No new PlayType.BLOCK. Reconciliation:
      count(SHOT outcome LIKE 'BLOCKED%') == sum(BoxScore.blocks).
    end note

    partition "BlockResolver (§3.7 — #025 D)" {
      note right
        A blocked ball is a **chaotic loose ball**, NOT the
        offenseRebound-vs-defenseRebound box-out contest — so
        recovery is a FLAT four-way roll (fixed weights, same
        for every block, defense-leaning). Weights are
        placeholders → calibrate empirically (~5 blocks/team).
      end note
      switch (recovery? //flat four-way roll (D)//)
      case (RECOVERED_OFFENSE)
        :in-bounds, offense retains
        → second-chance;
        stop
      case (RECOVERED_DEFENSE)
        :in-bounds, defense's ball
        → possession over;
        stop
      case (OOB_OFFENSE)
        :OOB off the blocker
        → offense retains → second-chance;
        stop
      case (OOB_DEFENSE)
        :OOB off the shooter
        → defense's ball → possession over;
        stop
      endswitch
    }
  else (no)
    if (shot made?\n//offense skill vs defense skill//\n//× acumen + teamOffense/teamDefense §3.4//\n//× fatigueFactor per player §3.5//) then (yes)
      :SHOT — MADE_*
      +2 or +3 points;
      partition "Assist (§3.4)" {
        if (assisted?\n//supporting-cast passing draw//) then (yes)
          :stamp assist_player_id
          credit assister;
        endif
      }
      partition "And-1 (§3.11 — decisions.md #029)" {
        note right
          **And-1 = a SECOND, post-make foul roll** (A1), carved
          BESIDE the assist — the pre-shot foul branch + BASE_FOUL
          are untouched, so this rate is independently tunable
          (the §3.7 block / §3.10 rebound-foul carve, a third time).
          A made basket already ended the possession → the and-1
          NEVER forks it; it only tacks on ONE FT (B). Coexists with
          the assist, doesn't interact (A3). Rate = rareEventProbability
          on AND_ONE_BASE + its own AND_ONE_SENSITIVITY (C).
        end note
        note right
          **§3.12 (decisions.md #030 A1/B) — SHIPPED.**
          §3.11's ``DRIVE or POST?`` gate here is **DELETED** — every
          made shot now rolls the and-1, and the graduation lives in
          the rate via the **SAME shared** foulMultiplier(shotType)
          table the pre-shot roll uses (B: one table, not two — the
          contact propensity is a property of the SHOT, not of which
          roll is asking). An and-1 on a THREE is rarer than a foul
          on a three **automatically**: the two rolls are independent
          and the shot must ALSO go in, so modeling it again would
          double-count it.
          **The two foul rolls are MUTUALLY EXCLUSIVE** — trace the
          flow above: the pre-shot FoulResolver branch **stops**, so a
          stopped shot never reaches here. One shot emits at most ONE
          of SHOOTING_FOUL / AND_ONE, never both, and the shared table
          is never applied twice to the same shot. The and-1 is
          conditioned TWICE (survived the foul roll, AND went in), so
          at §3.11's numbers a drive is ~15% stopped + ~2.6% and-1 —
          **~17.6% combined, not double**. Where they DO compound is
          the §3.10 period foul tally: both emit a FOUL and both count
          toward the bonus (and-1s alone moved fouls 3.95 → 4.41/team/
          period in §3.11). §3.12 roughly DOUBLES this roll's REACH
          — every made shot, not just made DRIVE/POST — but **MEASURED,
          the and-1 RATE rose only ~1.12× (1.67 → 1.87/team/game)**,
          because the shared multiplier lands TWICE in this path and
          compounds with the lower make rates. The tally channel is
          what the penalty-rate line (D) watches: 43.4% → 52.3% of
          team-periods in the penalty.
        end note
        if (and-1?\n//shooter foulDrawing vs defender discipline//\n//× foulMultiplier(shotType) §3.12 B — same table//\n//× defensivePressure; AND_ONE_SENSITIVITY (C)//\n//× fatigueFactor per player §3.5//) then (yes)
          if (**§3.14b — FLAGRANT?**\n//same shared roll (#034 A)//) then (yes)
            :FOUL — FLAGRANT_FOUL_1 or _2
            //15% severity sub-roll//; charge defender //recordFoul()//
            on _2: //recordFlagrantTwo()// → EJECTED;
            :FREE_THROW ×**2** — *_FLAGRANT
            the SHOOTER shoots (he was fouled, D)
            **2, not the and-1's 1 — replaces, doesn't add** (C);
            :**BASKET COUNTS + 2 FTs + OFFENSE RETAINS**
            → ``offensiveRebounds++; continue;`` (B)
            //(cap reached ⇒ possession ends, FTs still awarded)//
            **the ``stop`` below means "re-enters the loop", NOT "over"**;
            note right
              **THE CASE THAT MOST VISIBLY BREAKS #030 B** (#034 C).
              THREE scoring channels on ONE possession — the made FG,
              two free throws, AND the ball back. No other path in
              this engine produces that, it looks exactly like a
              double-count bug in a play-by-play, and **it is the
              rule**. #029 B's "the and-1 NEVER forks the possession —
              the make already ended it" is **superseded for the
              FLAGRANT case only**; the ordinary and-1 below is
              completely unchanged.
            end note
            stop
          endif
          :FOUL — AND_ONE
          charge defender foul (feeds foul-outs + §3.10 tally)
          committing_team_id = defTeamId (reuses #028 D column);
          :FREE_THROW — *_AND_ONE (source-tagged, D)
          ONE FT for the shooter (AND_ONE_FREE_THROWS = 1, B)
          **ALWAYS 1 — including a made THREE** (§3.12 C:
          3 pts + 1 FT, NOT 3 FTs — do not graduate this)
          +1 if made; FG points already recorded;
        endif
      }
      stop
    else (no)
      :SHOT — MISSED_*;
    endif
  endif
}

partition "Rebounding foul (§3.10 — decisions.md #028)" {
  note right
    **Carved off the TOP of the rebound phase** (C) — rolled BEFORE
    the board contest and SHORT-CIRCUITING it on a hit (the whistle
    stopped play, so nobody rebounds). Same shape as §3.7's block
    carve, which keeps this rate independently tunable — it never
    entangles with the rebound weights.
    **TWO-SIDED** (A2): a defensive box-out push (dominant) or an
    offensive over-the-back (the minority). The committer is drawn
    //foulProne//-weighted from the committing five, so the
    undisciplined bang bodies commit most of them.
    Rate = rareEventProbability(REBOUND_FOUL_BASE, …,
    REBOUND_FOUL_SENSITIVITY) × defensivePressure — floor-free,
    its own dial (the PROB_FLOOR trap, #028 impl note).
  end note
  if (rebounding foul?\n//aggregate foulDrawing vs (20 − foulProne)//\n//× defensivePressure; REBOUND_FOUL_SENSITIVITY//\n//× fatigueFactor per player §3.5//) then (yes)
    :FOUL — REBOUNDING_FOUL_DEFENSE or _OFFENSE
    charge committer foul (feeds foul-outs §3.5)
    committing_team_id = the committing side (#028 D);
    note right
      **EMIT-THEN-COUNT** (A1, the crux): the FOUL event is written
      FIRST, then GameData.isInBonus(committingTeam, period) reads
      the log — so the Nth foul (reaching BONUS_FOULS_PER_PERIOD = 5)
      **itself** sends the fouled team to the line. The penalty is
      **DERIVED from the FOUL events, never stored** — no teamFouls
      field, no reset logic (the #023-F / #013 / #015 discipline).
    end note
    if (**§3.14b — FLAGRANT?**\n//same shared roll (#034 A) — the ONLY site that//\n//can be committed by the OFFENSE (#028 A2, ~22%)//) then (yes)
      :FOUL — FLAGRANT_FOUL_1 or _2
      //15% severity sub-roll//; charge committer //recordFoul()//
      on _2: //recordFlagrantTwo()// → EJECTED;
      note right
        **The bonus is NOT consulted on a flagrant** — 2 FTs by
        rule, in the penalty or not (the #029 B shape). But the
        flagrant **DOES count toward the period tally** for the
        NEXT foul (#034 I): unlike §3.14a's technical it is a
        personal foul, so ``countsTowardBonus`` excludes it
        **not at all** and neither ``GameData.isInBonus`` nor
        the harness's independent tally changes.
        ⚠ **That non-change is deliberate, not accidental** —
        the exclusion lives in TWO derivations (#032's follow-up).
